{
  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "baseline": "934f9ee",
  "scope": "Grazing horizon guard for the native terrain land environment reflection, correcting the earlier black/background-gap diagnosis. Adds a deterministic survey-distance capture aid. Does not add material normals, new sky data, geometry or a second BRDF, and does not claim whole-frame visual acceptance.",
  "contract": {
    "problem": "The visible-normal GGX integral keeps rejected below-surface samples in the denominator. At a silhouette every sample can be rejected; Fresnel approaches one and removes the diffuse term, so final radiance is exactly zero and ridge crests tonemap black.",
    "guard": "env_specular_from computes horizon=1-smoothstep(0,0.2,N.V), floor=env_base_radiance(normal,ambient)*F*horizon, and returns max(integrated,floor).",
    "bounded": "The floor uses only the published environment field and the existing Schlick Fresnel. It adds no field, texture, pass, material coefficient or renormalization of surviving samples. It is zero at N.V>=0.2; the calibrated grazing oracle there is unchanged.",
    "diagnosis": "A constant-red fragment output removed the black pixels, proving they were shaded fragments rather than clear-colour/background holes. A fragment diagnostic found zero final radiance while albedo and illuminance were non-zero; the specular-off control removes the remaining dark rims, identifying them as reflected sky at grazing incidence.",
    "capture_aid": "--survey-distance 80..2000000 applies deterministic metres-after-reset framing for headless close-ups; rejected in flight, docking, map and vehicle-preview modes. It changes presentation only.",
    "unchanged": "Authoritative heights, geometry, material pages, simulation, contacts and render targets/passes are unchanged. No new persistent large allocation. Disabled specular still compiles the hook to zero."
  },
  "verification": {
    "status": "13 local command gates passed on 613 byte-identical compiled/configuration inputs; no remote CI claim",
