    "gpu_tests": [
      "grazing_floor_is_not_the_old_zero_early_return: a compute probe calls the actual shared environment.wgsl function with a uniform 100-radiance field at N.V=0, 1e-7 and 0.05. The pre-guard shader returns exactly zero at N.V=0, so this is a real regression. With the guard the three raw radiance values are 100, 99.99994 and 66.051, finite and bounded by the uniform field; N.V=0.2 remains the unfloored integrated value.",
      "extreme_grazing_terrain_environment_is_not_black: full primary raster on regular and conforming terrain at N.V=0.01, 0.001 and 0.0001, asserting every channel >=10. This exercises the integrated terrain path; it is not the exact pre-guard regression because the flat patch did not reproduce the black ridge, so the compute probe above carries that requirement.",
      "grazing_terrain_environment_remains_bounded: independent D*G*F solid-angle oracle at N.V=0.7 and 0.2, 8/255 envelope; values unchanged from the prior stage after the floor (0.2: actual 123/72 vs references 116/75; 0.7: 71/41 vs 71/39 for roughness 153/255).",
      "terrain_environment_ggx_matches_uniform_reference_and_releases_the_consumer: Low/Medium/High regular/conforming, tolerances 7/4/2; High values 101/77/31 for roughness 64/153/255.",
      "rough_terrain_blurs_environment_and_tracks_publication_without_material_uploads.",
      "terrain_reflected_cloud_budget_preserves_transport: actual [60,0,15] vs independent [63,0,15] on both grids, tolerance 8.",
      "terrain_environment_gpu_cost: counterbalanced disabled/Low/Medium/High, 32 samples each; latest medians 0.330/0.975/1.298/1.951 ms. Diagnostic only, not a budget or whole-client cost."
